  "id": "COMPOUND:15021 - PROTEIN:6324",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but consistent relationship between 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One and M-phase phosphoprotein 8. Multiple paths indicate that this compound acts as a target for SNU-387, which in turn is a target of various compounds, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside and 2-(2,6-Dihydroxyphenyl)-5-hydroxy-3,6,7-trimethoxychromen-4-one. All these compounds ultimately target M-phase phosphoprotein 8, suggesting a downstream effect on the cell cycle phase-specific protein. The evidence supports a mechanism where the compound may influence the cell cycle by modulating the activity of M-phase phosphoprotein 8, potentially through interactions with downstream signaling pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role in regulating cell cycle progression, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
